The transcriptions are converted from CMU's ARPAbet notation to IPA at build
time by app/tools/dictgen/lib/pron.mjs, and are General American — the variety
CMU recorded. This licence is permissive rather than share-alike, so unlike
sections 1-3 it imposes no obligation on files derived alongside it; the file is
kept separate anyway, so that every pack file remains traceable to exactly one
upstream.

A small number of readings in this file are written by hand rather than taken
from CMUdict, in app/tools/dictgen/corrections/en.readings.txt. They cover
headwords CMU has no entry for, which are almost all fragments the subtitle
corpus cut out of longer words ('t, didn, 'clock).


5. Glosses — not derived from any of the above sources
------------------------------------------------------

Files:  app/public/packs/*/gloss.*.txt
        app/public/packs/*/lex.txt
        app/public/packs/*/phrases.txt
        app/public/packs/*/phrases.*.txt

The glosses are generated at build time by a large language model, from the word
list alone. They are not copied or translated from any licensed dictionary or
corpus, and are not subject to the licences above. The phrase lists and their
glosses are written by hand for this project, from the same starting point.

lex.txt is listed here because it holds no meanings and no ranks: it is the
word list and its morphology, which is this project's own arrangement of its
own output.


